Hey there,
I had my problems with 4.14 too but after a few hours I got the hang of it.

I also used custom types for my collections and tried to create data with it.
To ensure compatibility with the new types I extended my custom types with the Strapi entities:
```typescript
import { Entity } from '@strapi/types/dist/modules/entity-service/index';
export interface CollectionA extends Entity<'api::collectiona.collectiona'> {
  // my old interface definition for faster rollback and testing
}
```

You can now use it as a result type when using the entity service (find, findMany).
```typescript
const result = strapi.entityService.findMany('api::collectiona.collectiona', {});
```
`result` now has the same fields as `CollectionA` and you can use it as the type. I used it to only change my types and not change my whole code basis.


To use the types as Input for `entityService.create` you have to use the `Input<'api::collectiona.collectiona'>` type.
This allows the creation of objects with references to other collections by strings, etc.
In your example:
```typescript
import { Input } from '@strapi/types/dist/modules/entity-service/params/data';

const newCollectionA: Input<'api::collectiona.collectiona'>= {
  textFieldA: "Hey",
  collectionB: <id of collection B>,
}
const createdItem = await strapi.entityService
.create("api::collectiona.collectiona", {
  data: {
    ...newCollectionA,
  },
  populate: {
    collectionB: true,
  },
})
```

I didn't test it on my machine but this should work.
If you have any further questions you can drop me an email.

